  "id": "aa26bd39-3ad1-5691-84c4-c6038d19e535",
  "slug": "italian-pastina-with-homemade-chicken-broth-recipe-12026854",
  "name": "Italian Pastina with Homemade Chicken Broth",
  "recipe_type": "soup",
  "brief_description": "Don\u2019t toss that chicken carcass! Use it to make homemade chicken stock for pastina, otherwise known as Italian penicillin, for its comforting properties. It\u2019s a hot, brothy chicken-and-vegetable soup poured over tiny pasta.",
  "cuisine": "Italian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Place chicken carcass in a large pot and add water. Cut 2 carrots and 2 celery stalks in half and add them to the pot along with 1 halved onion. Add salt and place pot over high heat. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, partially cover, and simmer for 35 to 45 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Strain stock and discard solids. Return stock to the pot."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Cut remaining carrots and celery in half and add them to the pot along with the remaining halved onion, bouillon, and garlic cloves. Place pot over medium-high heat and bring to a simmer. Cook, partially covered, for 45 minutes or until the vegetables are very tender."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Remove vegetables from the pot and place them in a blender along with 1 1/2 cups of broth."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Remove center insert from the blender lid to allow steam to escape and lightly cover the opening with a towel. Blend until very smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Pour all of the puree back into the broth and stir well. Return mixture to a simmer and cook for 10 to 15 minutes, while pasta is prepared. Add pepper and salt to taste."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Bring a pot of salted water to a boil and add pasta. Cook until just al dente, about 10 minutes. Drain."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Add about 2/3 cup pasta to a bowl and pour hot broth over. Top with plenty of grated Parmesan cheese, sprinkle with fresh parsley, and add more pepper if desired."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 90,
